# Nextra v4 Standards

## App Router Only

Nextra v4 uses Next.js App Router exclusively. Pages Router is discontinued.

- Place MDX files in `content/` directory (catch-all route) or use `page.{md,mdx}` convention
- Add `app/[[...mdxPath]]/page.jsx` as the gateway to the `content/` directory

## Layout Setup

```jsx
// app/layout.jsx
import { Footer, Layout, Navbar } from 'nextra-theme-docs'
import { Banner, Head } from 'nextra/components'
import { getPageMap } from 'nextra/page-map'
import 'nextra-theme-docs/style.css' // Required – no longer auto-imported

export default async function RootLayout({ children }) {
  return (
    <html lang="en" dir="ltr" suppressHydrationWarning>
      <Head />
      <body>
        <Layout
          navbar={<Navbar logo={<b>My Docs</b>} projectLink="..." />}
          pageMap={await getPageMap()}
          footer={<Footer>MIT {new Date().getFullYear()}</Footer>}
        >
          {children}
        </Layout>
      </body>
    </html>
  )
}
```

## MDX Components

```jsx
// mdx-components.jsx (required at project root)
import { useMDXComponents as getDocsMDXComponents } from 'nextra-theme-docs'

const docsComponents = getDocsMDXComponents()

export function useMDXComponents(components) {
  return { ...docsComponents, ...components }
}
```

## No `theme.config` Files

`theme.config` is removed. Pass all options as props to `<Layout>`, `<Navbar>`, `<Footer>`, `<Banner>`, and `<Search>` in `app/layout.jsx`.

## Search (Pagefind)

FlexSearch is replaced by Pagefind (Rust-powered).

```json
// package.json
"scripts": {
  "postbuild": "pagefind --site .next/server/app --output-path public/_pagefind"
}
```

Add `_pagefind/` to `.gitignore`.

## Metadata / Front Matter

Use Next.js Metadata API. Front matter is exported as `metadata` automatically.

```mdx
---
title: My Page
description: Page description
---
```

Do NOT mix front matter and `export const metadata` in the same file.

## Renamed / Moved APIs

| Old (v3) | New (v4) |
|---|---|
| `<RemoteContent>` from `nextra/components` | `<MDXRemote>` from `nextra/mdx-remote` |
| `useRouter` from `nextra/hooks` | `useRouter` from `next/navigation` |
| `<Th>`, `<Tr>`, `<Td>` | `<Table.Th>`, `<Table.Tr>`, `<Table.Td>` |
| `compileMdx` returns `{ result }` | Returns `Promise<string>` directly |

## `_meta` Files

- Must be server components (no `'use client'`)
- Use `_meta.global.js` to define all pages in one file (cannot mix with per-folder `_meta`)
- External links auto-open in new tab with `↗` icon

### Hidden Pages

To make a page accessible via its URL but hidden from the sidebar, use `display: 'hidden'` in `_meta.js`:

```javascript
export default {
  agent_workspace: 'Agent Workspace',
  twilio_webchat: {
    display: 'hidden',
    title: 'Twilio Flex WebChat',
  },
}
```

This is the Nextra equivalent of Hugo's `[_build] list = 'never'` / `noindex = true`.

### Folder Index Pages (`asIndexPage`)

When a folder has an `index.mdx` that serves as its landing page, use `asIndexPage: true` in the front matter. This makes the folder clickable in the sidebar without creating a duplicate child entry.

**Never** add `index` as a key in the folder's `_meta.js` — that causes the index page to appear twice.

```mdx
❌ _meta.js has: index: 'Browser Agent SDK'
   → "Browser Agent SDK" appears as folder label AND as first child item

✅ index.mdx front matter has: asIndexPage: true
   → Folder is clickable; no duplicate child item
```

```mdx
---
title: Browser Agent SDK
description: ...
asIndexPage: true
---
```

```javascript
// browseragent/_meta.js — omit `index` entirely
export default {
  reference: 'SDK Reference',
}
```

## Cards Component

`Cards` and `Cards.Card` are available from `nextra/components` and render a responsive CSS grid of clickable link cards.

```mdx
import { Cards } from 'nextra/components'

<Cards num={2}>
  <Cards.Card title="iOS SDK" href="https://example.com" arrow>
    Core features for implementing event handling without a UI.
  </Cards.Card>
  <Cards.Card title="iOS Default UI SDK" href="https://example.com" arrow>
    Out-of-the-box implementation with a default UI and sample app.
  </Cards.Card>
</Cards>
```

### `num` Prop — Always Set Explicitly

| Use case | Recommended `num` |
|---|---|
| 2 cards or 2-column layout | `num={2}` |
| 3 cards or 3-column layout | `num={3}` |
| 4 cards (2×2 grid) | `num={2}` |

```mdx
❌ <Cards>              — default num={3}, cards too narrow for description text
✅ <Cards num={2}>      — wider cards, description text has room to breathe
```

### External Links in Cards

For cards linking to external URLs, pass `target` and `rel` as props:

```mdx
<Cards.Card
  title="Android SDK"
  href="https://gitlab.com/..."
  target="_blank"
  rel="noreferrer"
  arrow
>
  Description text here.
</Cards.Card>
```

Nextra's auto-`target="_blank"` behaviour does **not** apply inside `Cards.Card href` — set it manually.

## Tailwind CSS 4 Prefix

